    "short_label": {
      "en": "$txcin_upthres2"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "This is the upper limit of the second USC income band, used as the band_uplim parameter in the txcin_ie SchedCalc function for the 'Tax schedule: basic rates'. Income between Threshold 1 and this threshold is charged at Rate 2 ($txcin_rate2, 2%). The Country Report shows this threshold rising over time - €21,295 (2022), €22,920 (2023), €25,760 (2024), €27,382 (2025) - consistent with the constant's latest recorded value of €28,700 and its 13 historical entries, reflecting periodic upward uprating (e.g. Budget increases to keep more income in the lower bands)."
    },
    "explanation": {
      "en": "EUROMOD function group: SICs and tax constants"
    },
